Mickey Hub licensing
====================

Copyright 2026 Mickey Hub contributors.

Mickey Hub's first-party work is source-available under the public licenses
below, with a separate limited commercial permission in COMMERCIAL_USE.md.
This scope notice does not modify the complete standard license texts.

Designs, models, documentation and media
---------------------------------------

Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International
SPDX: CC-BY-NC-4.0
Complete, unmodified text: LICENSES/CC-BY-NC-4.0.txt

This covers copyrightable first-party enclosure and board designs, original
model contributions, STL exports, drawings, documentation and presentation
media, including first-party contributions to the integrated Blender model.

Firmware and software tools
---------------------------

PolyForm Noncommercial License 1.0.0
SPDX: PolyForm-Noncommercial-1.0.0
Complete, unmodified text: LICENSES/PolyForm-Noncommercial-1.0.0.md

This covers first-party firmware and software tools, including corresponding
first-party contributions to supplied build artifacts.

Required Notice: Copyright 2026 Mickey Hub contributors.

Limited commercial permission
-----------------------------

The applicable public licenses permit noncommercial development, modification,
sharing, personal builds and noncommercial prototypes under their terms.

COMMERCIAL_USE.md additionally permits the same individual or legal entity
to sell up to and including 100 covered units per calendar year without a
license fee or an individual authorization request. A covered unit is one
complete Mickey Hub or derived device, or one kit for assembling it. Count
all of the entity's brands, stores, channels and variants together.

The grant covers associated first-party design and software use under its
conditions. Before selling the 101st unit in that year, obtain a separate
written commercial license. The year runs from January 1 through December 31.

Request authorization from the Reactor maintainers at:
phyreact@gmail.com

Contact alone is not authorization. See COMMERCIAL_USE.md for the complete
additional grant and counting rules. The original public licenses remain
independently available for uses they permit.

Exclusions and mixed works
-------------------------

Third-party software, manufacturer documents, purchased-module CAD, libraries,
icons, fonts and separately licensed assets retain their original notices and
terms. For mixed assemblies, these licenses cover only first-party work.

The ST driver in firmware/zero/tof/vendor/ retains its original license.
LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt supplies the standard text for Apache-licensed
third-party dependencies; it does not license Mickey Hub's first-party work.
Pico SDK retains LICENSES/Pico-SDK-BSD-3-Clause.txt. Manufacturer material in
components/references/, components/datasheets/ and local KiCad libraries is
not relicensed by this file.

A Reactor commercial authorization covers only rights held or controlled by
its grantor. Microduck and other third-party assets may require independent
permissions from their rights holders. See THIRD_PARTY.md and ../LICENSING.md.
